README.Roadmap
==============

Project: Retrospective testing of DOCK 6 -- automation of scripts, test set
         growth, and generation of statistics/tables for the paper.

This file is a living plan.  Edit it by hand as ideas change.
Status markers:  [ ] not started   [~] in progress   [x] done


GOALS
-----
1. Make the existing (mostly csh) scripts robust so they no longer need
   hand-holding.
2. Translate the csh scripts to Python.  SLURM submission scripts stay csh
   and are wrapped/launched by Python.
3. Make it easy to add new systems to the test set in a semi-automated way.
4. Allow choosing between a FULL rerun (e.g. after a DOCK code change) and a
   run on only the newly added systems, then regenerate all tables.
5. Automatically generate the tables (and numbers) needed for the paper.
6. Define environment variables in one setup file created at setup time.


GUIDING PRINCIPLES
------------------
- Target version: ALL tests are evaluated on DOCK 6.14 (not yet released as
  of 2026-11-24).  Until release, development and script testing use a
  pre-release/development build; final paper numbers must be regenerated
  with the released 6.14.  Record the exact DOCK version/build in settings.txt
  and in every results directory so tables can be traced to a build.
- Human-readable plain text for manifests, settings, and tables.
  No YAML.  Use '#' comments, whitespace/tab-delimited columns, key = value.
- Keep code simple and easy to edit by hand.  The author wants to tweak
  scripts as we go; build on hand edits, never overwrite them.
- Preserve behavior when translating.  List intentional changes separately
  so results in the paper do not change by accident.
- Nothing is compiled, executed, or submitted without confirming first.
- Use --dry-run style options wherever a script launches work.


PROJECT STRUCTURE: FOUR PARTS
-----------------------------
The work divides into two related but separate themes, each with two parts:

  Theme A -- Test sets
    Part 1. Test set CONSTRUCTION
            Building new test sets (preparing receptors/ligands, building
            missing protein pieces, adding systems to the manifest).
    Part 2. EXISTING test sets
            Using published/established sets (SB2010, SB2012, SB2025,
            DT1244, DT100, ...) as they are.

  Theme B -- DOCK features
    Part 3. Implemented FEATURES in DOCK 6.14
            What was added/changed in DOCK (e.g. macrocycle docking,
            covalent minimization, HDB covalent, crosslinker docking).
    Part 4. TESTING the features with the test sets
            Running Part 3 features on Part 1/2 test sets and generating
            the paper's tables.

Each paper section below should be tagged with the part(s) it belongs to.
Tentative tagging (author to correct):
    Macrocycle docking .................. Part 3 feature, Part 4 test;
                                          test set (Y. S. Tan, in progress) is
                                          Part 1 construction
    Covalent minimization / HDB covalent  Part 3 feature, Part 4 test
    RAS test set ........................ Part 1 or 2 (construction vs
                                          existing -- to clarify)
    Covalent test set ................... Part 1 or 2 (to clarify)
    Build missing parts of proteins ..... Part 1 (construction) and/or Part 3
    Dock crosslinking molecules ......... Part 3 feature, Part 4 test
    SB2010 / SB2025 / DT1244 / DT100 .... Part 2 (existing)

Design implication: test sets (Parts 1-2) are the "systems" in the manifest;
features (Part 3) are the "experiments" run on them (Part 4).  A results
directory is therefore keyed by DOCK version + feature/experiment + test
set, and the manifest should record which test set each system belongs to.


